From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] rocket: rk3576: fused RELU, first-conv 0x4050 and
 unsupported small-channel convs

 - Fused RELU / RELU6: rocket programmed no activation and relied on the
   output range, which only holds when the output zero point is the
   type's minimum. A tensor that shares its quantisation with another one
   (a CONCATENATION input) has the zero point inside the range, and the
   negative half came out unclamped. Use the vendor's DPU BN stage RELU
   (0x4060 = 0x902, lower bounds 0) with the output lift 0 so that the
   clamp sits at a real 0.
 - First conv 0x4050: bit 8 follows the parity of the 16-channel output
   groups, as on the regular path. The encoder had one fixed word per
   bias mode, so every first conv of the other parity came back flat
   (<= 16 outputs, and int8 per-tensor with 17..32 outputs).
 - Convolutions with <= 4 input channels that the first-conv encoder does
   not cover (1x1, 2 or 4 channels, ...) would read first-conv buffers
   with the generic encoder; leave them to the CPU.

Checked with a generated sweep of 894 small models (input conv shapes,
concatenation inputs, kernels 3/5/7, stride 1/2): 892 within one step of
TFLite, the other two at rounding level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
